.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBSplitter\fR: panes along one axis with a draggable handle between each pair, after Mantine's Splitter. The sizing rules (fixed and flexible panes, limits, collapsing, redistribution) are the \fBsplitter\fR primitive; this lays the panes out, draws the handles and turns a drag into events.
.PP
Controlled: the app owns one \fBSplitterState\fR and applies the one message the widget speaks:
.PP
.nf
.RS
// state: panes with their sizes and limits
SplitterState::new(vec![
    Pane::fixed(240.0).min(Limit::Px(160.0)).collapsible(true),   // a sidebar
    Pane::flex(),
])

// view
Splitter::new(&self.split).pane(sidebar).pane(content).on_event(Msg::Split)

// update
Msg::Split(event) => { self.split.apply(event); }
// from code: self.split.toggle(0)
.RE
.fi
.PP
Panes are the widget's children, in order, one per pane of the state. The handle is a hairline with a small grip (\fBwith_handle\fR hides the grip; the line stays and still drags), \fBline_size\fR its thickness. Splitters nest: put one in a pane. Give it a bounded height (and width); it fills what it is given. Moving a handle with the keyboard is not included: iced has no focus model to hang it on.
